      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C69"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "Aqueous solubility and formulation for the query are unspecified; logD 5.24 suggests dissolution risk.",
    "First-pass metabolism, efflux transport, and N-oxide reduction are not experimentally characterized.",
    "L3 oral exposure records lack IV comparators and are for reference molecules, not the query; structural transfer is qualitative.",
    "No query-specific AUC/Cmax data."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L1/L2 direct and cross-species F values for lipophilic heteroaromatic reference drugs (vismodegib 31.8%, celecoxib 22-40%, bosentan ~50%, erlotinib 59%) support F>=20% for the query despite high logD. L3 oral exposure adds only indirect support (erlotinib AUC∞ 10.2 µg·h/mL after 150 mg) and no query-specific or threshold-relevant negative evidence. The single sub-20% mouse value (GSK269984A ~14%) is low-transfer and internally contradicted. Prediction remains high, confidence moderate."
}

